      <h2 id="nodes-cluster-enabling-features-install_nodes-cluster-enabling" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling feature sets at installation<a href="#nodes-cluster-enabling-features-install_nodes-cluster-enabling" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can enable feature sets for all nodes in the cluster by editing the <code>install-config.yaml</code> file before you deploy the cluster. This allows you to use non-default features in your cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have an <code>install-config.yaml</code> file.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Use the <code>featureSet</code> parameter to specify the name of the feature set you want to enable, such as <code>TechPreviewNoUpgrade</code>:
      <Alert variant="warning" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Warning</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Enabling the <code>TechPreviewNoUpgrade</code> feature set on your cluster cannot be undone and prevents minor version updates. You should not enable this feature set on production clusters.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <CodeBlock code={"compute:\n- hyperthreading: Enabled\n  name: worker\n  platform:\n    aws:\n      rootVolume:\n        iops: 2000\n        size: 500\n        type: io1\n      metadataService:\n        authentication: Optional\n      type: c5.4xlarge\n      zones:\n      - us-west-2c\n  replicas: 3\nfeatureSet: TechPreviewNoUpgrade"} lang="yaml" title="Sample install-config.yaml file with an enabled feature set" />
      <ol><li>Save the file and reference it when using the installation program to deploy the cluster.</li></ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <p>You can verify that the feature gates are enabled by looking at the <code>kubelet.conf</code> file on a node after the nodes return to the ready state.</p>
      <ol>
      <li>From the <strong>Administrator</strong> perspective in the web console, navigate to <strong>Compute</strong> -&gt; <strong>Nodes</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select a node.</li>
      <li>In the <strong>Node details</strong> page, click <strong>Terminal</strong>.</li>
      <li>
      In the terminal window, change your root directory to <code>/host</code>:
      <CodeBlock code={"sh-4.2# chroot /host"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      View the <code>kubelet.conf</code> file:
      <CodeBlock code={"sh-4.2# cat /etc/kubernetes/kubelet.conf"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"# ...\nfeatureGates:\n  InsightsOperatorPullingSCA: true,\n  LegacyNodeRoleBehavior: false\n# ..."} lang="terminal" title="Sample output" />
      <p>The features that are listed as <code>true</code> are enabled on your cluster.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>The features listed vary depending upon the OpenShift Container Platform version.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
